2026-11-06T08:13:53.3485390Z LLD and LLDB are now provided in separate formulae:
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3587420Z   brew install lld
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3636860Z   brew install lldb
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3666190Z 
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3769000Z Z3 solver support will be removed in LLVM 24 as it is unsupported upstream,
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3817980Z see https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/205370
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3820950Z 
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3823150Z Using `clang`, `clang++`, etc., requires a CLT installation at `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools`.
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3835580Z If you don't want to install the CLT, you can write appropriate configuration files pointing to your
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3938010Z SDK at ~/.config/clang.
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3962890Z 
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3963720Z To use the bundled libunwind please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3964270Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3964540Z 
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3964770Z To use the bundled libc++ please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3965720Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/c++ -L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3966390Z Features newer than system libc++ will require the following define to enable
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3966910Z (support for this may be removed in a future major LLVM release):
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3967330Z   CPPFLAGS="-D_LIBCPP_DISABLE_AVAILABILITY"
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3967550Z 
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3967890Z NOTE: You probably want to use the libunwind and libc++ provided by macOS unless you know what you're doing.
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3968280Z 
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3968430Z llvm is keg-only, which means it was not symlinked into /opt/homebrew,
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3968980Z because macOS already provides this software and installing another version in
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3969470Z parallel can cause all kinds of trouble.
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3969690Z 
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3969790Z If you need to have llvm first in your PATH, run:
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3970360Z   printf '%s\n' export\ PATH\=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin:\$PATH >> /Users/runner/.bash_profile
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3970710Z 
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3970890Z For compilers to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3972270Z   export LDFLAGS=-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3972800Z   export CPPFLAGS=-I/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/include
2026-11-06T08:13:53.3973100Z 
